  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.2.1\"\n\npackage:\n  name: sphn\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/s/sphn/sphn-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 3b19b1fece67d979d84080458bed545d1f55ddc5abac6ca5deae2672a184c7fe\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script:\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses --format yaml --output THIRDPARTY.yml\n    - ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - if: build_platform != target_platform\n      then:\n        - python\n        - cross-python_${{ target_platform }}\n        - maturin >=1.4,<2\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib('c') }}\n    - ${{ compiler('rust') }}\n    - cargo-bundle-licenses\n    - pkg-config\n  host:\n    - python\n    - pip\n    - maturin >=1.4,<2\n    - libopus\n  run:\n    - python\n    - numpy\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - sphn\n        - sphn.sphn\n      pip_check: true\n  - requirements:\n      run:\n        - numpy\n    script:\n      - python test_roundtrip.py\n    files:\n      recipe:\n        - test_roundtrip.py\n\nabout:\n  summary: Python bindings to read/write audio files via the symphonia and opus crates\n  description: |\n    sphn provides Python bindings for the symphonia and opus Rust crates.\n    It can load a variety of audio file formats into numpy arrays and\n    read/write ogg/opus audio files with streaming support.\n  license: Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE\n    - THIRDPARTY.yml\n  homepage: https://github.com/LaurentMazare/sphn\n  repository: https://github.com/LaurentMazare/sphn\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - eginhard\n",
